From 76ffd677975c8d68048cc551030e14e7470348ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:43:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Build a real Linktree CMS with live preview, in the
 sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds "Social Media x Linktree" back to the sidebar, but pointing at
a CMS editor (public/linktree-admin.html), not the public page — the
public linktree.html itself stays bare, unwrapped, for social bio
visitors.

- public/linktree-admin.html — form to edit tagline, both stats, the
  full link list (add/remove/reorder/edit, badge style + text), and
  footer fields, with a live phone-sized preview panel that updates
  as you type. Save button hits the API below.
- lib/linktree-store.js — reads/writes the config via Vercel Blob
  storage (@vercel/blob). Falls back to DEFAULT_CONFIG (the same
  content that used to be hardcoded) until Blob is connected or
  before the first save, so nothing breaks in the meantime.
- pages/api/linktree/config.js — GET returns the current config,
  PUT saves it.
- public/linktree.html — now fetches /api/linktree/config at load
  instead of the static linktree-config.js (removed, superseded by
  the store).

Setup needed before Save actually persists: open this project in the
Vercel dashboard, go to Storage, create/connect a Blob store. Vercel
auto-adds the BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN env var when you do — no token
to create by hand. Until that's done, the CMS still loads and
previews fine, but Save will fail (the store falls back to defaults
on every load rather than actually persisting).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
